	(195, 1, '2024-05-28 10:08:31', '2024-05-28 02:08:31', '<!-- wp:media-text {"mediaId":11,"mediaType":"image","className":"is-style-default"} -->\n<div class="wp-block-media-text is-stacked-on-mobile is-style-default"><figure class="wp-block-media-text__media"><img src="http://localhost/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/EDITED-IMG_0198-edited-scaled.jpg" alt="DA-CBC Front Image of the building" class="wp-image-11 size-full"/></figure><div class="wp-block-media-text__content"><!-- wp:paragraph {"placeholder":"Content…"} -->\n<p>The <strong>Crop Biotechnology Center (CBC) </strong>is one of three biotechnology centers under the <strong>Department of Agriculture </strong>(DA). It serves as a catalyst in the development of and utilization of modern biotechnologies for agriculture. It rationalizes and implements the research, development, and extension agenda of the DA-Biotech Program. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:media-text -->\n\n<!-- wp:block {"ref":192} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>It also provides biotechnology capacity-building services to a network of R4D institution in the use of modern crop biotechnologies. <strong>DA-CBC</strong> focuses on applying advanced technologies that contribute to the improvement in performance, yield, and quality of important commodities, such as rice, corn, coconut, and high value crops, such as mango, garlic, onion, eggplant, tomato, cotton, rubber, cassava, sweet potato, yam, cacao, papaya, banana, and abaca.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:block {"ref":192} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:details -->\n<details class="wp-block-details"><summary><strong>R4D AREAS</strong></summary><!-- wp:list -->\n<ul><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Genetics</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Genetic Engineering and Gene Editing</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Tissue Culture</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Microbial Biotechnology</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!--