g>Systems Biology (\'omics\')</strong></summary><!-- wp:list -->\n<ul><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Systems biology approaches combining metabolomics with proteomics and/or transcriptomics</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Experimental strategies to characterize ribonucleic acid-protein complexes/interactions</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list --></details>\n<!-- /wp:details -->\n\n<!-- wp:details {"showContent":true} -->\n<details class="wp-block-details" open><summary><strong>Microbial Biotechnology</strong></summary><!-- wp:list -->\n<ul><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Use of plant-growth-promoting microorganisms (PGPM) as biofertilizers to enhance plant and soil health and biopesticide to control invasive plants and insects</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list --></details>\n<!-- /wp:details -->\n\n<!-- wp:details {"showContent":true} -->\n<details class="wp-block-details" open><summary><strong><strong>Bioinformatics and Computational Biology</strong></strong></summary><!-- wp:list -->\n<ul><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Use of bioinformatics tools and high-performance computing systems and various computing support services to transform complex data into information useful to scientists</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list --></details>\n<!-- /wp:details -->\n\n<!-- wp:details {"showContent":true} -->\n<details class="wp-block-details" open><summary><strong>Molecular Diagnostic</strong></summary><!-- wp:list -->\n<ul><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Development of molecular tests, including biochemical, electrochemical, optical, and imaging-based, to diagnose diseases or other pathological conditions</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list --></details>\n<!-- /wp:details --></details>\n<!-- /wp:details -->\n\n<!-- wp:block {"ref":192} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:details -->\n<details class="wp-block-details"><summary><strong>TRAINING/ CONFERENCE VENUE</strong></summary><!-- wp:media-text {"mediaPosition":"right","mediaId":213,"mediaLink":"http://localhost/cbc-2021-9september-plenary-hall-audience-view-1/","mediaType":"image","verticalAlignment":"center","imageFill":true} -->\n<div class="wp-block-media-text has-media-on-the-right is-stacked-on-mobile is-vertically-aligned-center is-image-fill"><div class="wp-block-media-text__content"><!-- wp:paragraph {"placeholder":"Content…"} -->\n<p>Plenary Hall (Capacity:600 pax) </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><figure class="wp-block-media-text__media" style="background-image:url(http://localhost/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/CBC-2021-9September-Plenary-Hall-audience-view-1-1024x683.jpg);background-position:50% 50%"><img src="http://localhost/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/CBC-2021-9September-Plenary-Hall-audience-view-1-1024x683.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-213 size-full"/></figure></div>\n<!-- /wp:media-text -->\n\n<!-- wp:block {"ref":192} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:media-text {"mediaPosition":"right","mediaId":219,"mediaLink":"http://localhost/cbc-2021-9september-multipurpose-hall/","mediaType":"image","verticalAlignment":"center","imageFill":true} -->\n<div class="wp-block-media-text has-media-on-the-right is-stacked-on-mobile is-vertically-aligned-center is-image-fill"><div class="wp-block-media-text__content"><!-- wp:paragraph {"placeholder":"Content…"} -->\n<p>Multipurpose Hall (Сарасіtу: 300 рах)</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><figure class="wp-block-media-text__media" style="background-image:url(http://localhost/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/CBC-2021-9September-Multipurpose-Hall-1024x683.jpg);background-position:50% 50%"><img src="http://localhost/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/CBC-2021-9September-Multipurpose-Hall-1024x683.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-219 size-full"/></figure></div>\n<!-- /wp:media-text -->\n\n<!-- wp:block {"ref":192} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:media-text {"mediaPosition":"right","mediaId":215,"mediaLink":"http://localhost/cbc-2021-9september-office-1st-flr/","mediaType":"image","verticalAlignment":"center","imageFill":true} -->\n<div class="wp-block-media-text has-media-on-the-right is-stacked-on-mobile is-vertically-aligned-center is-image-fill"><div class="wp-block-media-text__content"><!-- wp:paragraph {"placeholder":"Content…"} -->\n<p>Training Rooms (Capacity: 300 pax)</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><figure class="wp-block-media-text__media" style="background-image:url(http://localhost/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/CBC-2021-9September-Office-1st-Flr-1024x461.jpg);background-position:50% 50%"><img src="http://localhost/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/CBC-2021-9September-Office-1st-Flr-1024x461.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-215 size-full"/></figure></div>\n<!-- /wp:media-text --></details>\n<!-- /wp:details -->\n\n<!-- wp:block {"ref":192} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:html -->\n\n<div id="accordion-collapse" data-accordion="collapse">\n  <h2 id="accordion-collapse-heading-1">\n    <button type="button" class="flex items-center justify-between w-full p-5 font-medium rtl:text-right text-gray-500 border border-b-0 border-gray-200 rounded-t-xl focus:ring-4 focus:ring-gray-200 dark:focus:ring-gray-800 dark:border-gray-700 dark:text-gray-400 hover:bg-gray-100 dark:hover:bg-gray-800 gap-3" data-accordion-target="#accordion-collapse-body-1" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="accordion-collapse-body-1">\n      <span>What is Flowbite?</span>\n      <svg data-accordion-icon class="w-3 h-3 rotate-180 shrink-0" aria-hidden="true" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 10 6">\n        <path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 5 5 1 1 5"/>\n      </svg>\n    </button>\n  </h2>\n  <div id="accordion-collapse-body-1" class="hidden" aria-labelledby="accordion-collapse-heading-1">\n    <div class="p-5 border border-b-0 border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 dark:bg-gray-900">\n      <p class="mb-2 text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">Flowbite is an open-source library of interactive components built on top of Tailwind CSS including buttons, dropdowns, modals, navbars, and more.</p>\n      <p class="text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">Check out this guide to learn how to <a href="/docs/getting-started/introduction/" class="text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-500 hover:underline">get started</a> and start developing websites even faster with components on top of Tailwind CSS.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <h2 id="accordion-collapse-heading-2">\n    <button type="button" class="flex items-center justify-between w-full p-5 font-medium rtl:text-right text-gray-500 border border-b-0 border-gray-200 focus:ring-4 focus:ring-gray-200 dark:focus:ring-gray-800 dark:border-gray-700 dark:text-gray-400 hover:bg-gray-100 dark:hover:bg-gray-800 gap-3" data-accordion-target="#accordion-collapse-body-2" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="accordion-collapse-body-2">\n      <span>Is there a Figma file available?</span>\n      <svg data-accordion-icon class="w-3 h-3 rotate-180 shrink-0" aria-hidden="true" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 10 6">\n        <path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 5 5 1 1 5"/>\n      </svg>\n    </button>\n  </h2>\n  <div id="accordion-collapse-body-2" class="hidden" aria-labelledby="accordion-collapse-heading-2">\n    <div class="p-5 border border-b-0 border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">\n      <p class="mb-2 text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">Flowbite is first conceptualized and designed using the Figma software so everything you see in the library has a design equivalent in our Figma file.</p>\n      <p class="text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">Check out the <a href="https://flowbite.com/figma/" class="text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-500 hover:underline">Figma design system</a> based on the utility classes from Tailwind CSS and components from Flowbite.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <h2 id="accordion-collapse-heading-3">\n    <button type="button" class="flex items-center justify-between w-full p-5 font-medium rtl:text-right text-gray-500 border border-gray-200 focus:ring-4 focus:ring-gray-200 dark:focus:ring-gray-800 dark:border-gray-700 dark:text-gray-400 hover:bg-gray-100 dark:hover:bg-gray-800 gap-3" data-accordion-target="#accordion-collapse-body-3" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="accordion-collapse-body-3">\n      <span>What are the differences between Flowbite and Tailwind UI?</span>\n      <svg data-accordion-icon class="w-3 h-3 rotate-180 shrink-0" aria-hidden="true" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 10 6">\n        <path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 5 5 1 1 5"/>\n      </svg>\n    </button>\n  </h2>\n  <div id="accordion-collapse-body-3" class="hidden" aria-labelledby="accordion-collapse-heading-3">\n    <div class="p-5 border border-t-0 border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">\n      <p class="mb-2 text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">The main difference is that the core components from Flowbite are open source under the MIT license, whereas Tailwind UI is a paid product. Another difference is that Flowbite relies on smaller and standalone components, whereas Tailwind UI offers sections of pages.</p>\n      <p class="mb-2 text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">However, we actually recommend using both Flowbite, Flowbite Pro, and even Tailwind UI as there is no technical reason stopping you from using the best of two worlds.</p>\n      <p class="mb-2 text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">Learn more about these technologies:</p>\n      <ul class="ps-5 text-gray-500 list-disc dark:text-gray-400">\n        <li><a href="https://flowbite.com/pro/" class="text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-500 hover:underline">Flowbite Pro</a></li>\n        <li><a href="https://tailwindui.com/" rel="nofollow" class="text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-500 hover:underline">Tailwind UI</a></li>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<!-- /wp:html -->', 'What is DA-CBC?', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '152-revision-v1', '', '', '2024-05-28 11:28:27', '2024-05-28 03:28:27', '', 152, 'http://localhost/?p=254', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
	(255, 1, '2024-05-28 11:29:57', '2024-05-28 03:29:57', '<!-- wp:media-text {"mediaId":11,"mediaType":"image"} -->\n<div class="wp-block-media-text is-stacked-on-mobile"><figure class="wp-block-media-text__media"><img src="http://localhost/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/EDITED-IMG_0198-edited-scaled.jpg" alt="DA-CBC Front Image of the building" class="wp-image-11 size-full"/></figure><div class="wp-block-media-text__content"><!-- wp:paragraph {"placeholder":"Content…"} -->\n<p>The <strong>Crop Biotechnology Center (CBC) </strong>is one of three biotechnology centers under the <strong>Department of Agriculture </strong>(DA). It serves as a catalyst in the development of and utilization of modern biotechnologies for agriculture. It rationalizes and implements the research, development, and extension agenda of the DA-Biotech Program. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:media-text -->\n\n<!-- wp:block {"ref":192} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>It also provides biotechnology capacity-building services to a network of R4D institution in the use of modern crop biotechnologies. <strong>DA-CBC</strong> focuses on applying advanced technologies that contribute to the improvement in performance, yield, and quality of important commodities, such as rice, corn, coconut, and high value crops, such as mango, garlic, onion, eggplant, tomato, cotton, rubber, cassava, sweet potato, yam, cacao, papaya, banana, and abaca.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:block {"ref":192} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:details -->\n<details class="wp-block-details"><summary><strong>R4D AREAS</strong></summary><!-- wp:list -->\n<ul><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Genetics</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Genetic Engineering and Gene Editing</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Tissue Culture</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Microbial Biotechnology</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Diagnostics</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Bioinformatics and Computational Biology</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Natural Products, Natural Ingredients, and Value-Adding</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list --></details>\n<!-- /wp:details -->\n\n<!-- wp:block {"ref":192} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:details -->\n<details class="wp-block-details"><summary><strong>LABORATORIES</strong></summary><!-- wp:details {"showContent":true} -->\n<details class="wp-block-details" open><summary><strong>Molecular Genetics</strong></summary><!-- wp:list -->\n<ul><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Functional genomic approaches to accelerate crop breeding and production</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Construction of detailed, high-resolution QTL maps and physical maps for map-based cloning</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list --></details>\n<!-- /wp:details -->\n\n<!-- wp:details {"showContent":true} -->\n<details class="wp-block-details" open><summary><strong>Genetic Transformation</strong></summary><!-- wp:list -->\n<ul><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Use of genetic manipulation to improve traits of interest<strong> </strong></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Development of genetically modified (GM) and non-GM organisms, alterations to gene sequences, and gene knock-outs (RNAi)</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list --></details>\n<!-- /wp:details -->\n\n<!-- wp:details {"showContent":true} -->\n<details class="wp-block-details" open><summary><strong>Tissue Culture</strong></summary><!-- wp:list -->\n<ul><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Aseptic propagation of plant parts in a highly controlled environment</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Creation of genetic variability for crop improvement</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list --></details>\n<!-- /wp:details -->\n\n<!-- wp:details {"showContent":true} -->\n<details class="wp-block-details" open><summary><strong>Systems Biology (\'omics\')</strong></summary><!-- wp:list -->\n<ul><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Systems biology approaches combining metabolomics with proteomics and/or transcriptomics</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Experimental strategies to characterize ribonucleic acid-protein complexes/interactions</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list --></details>\n<!-- /wp:details -->\n\n<!-- wp:details {"showContent":true} -->\n<details class="wp-block-details" open><summary><strong>Microbial Biotechnology</strong></summary><!-- wp:list -->\n<ul><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Use of plant-growth-promoting microorganisms (PGPM) as biofertilizers to enhance plant and soil health and biopesticide to control invasive plants and insects</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list --></details>\n<!-- /wp:details -->\n\n<!-- wp:details {"showContent":true} -->\n<details class="wp-block-details" open><summary><strong><strong>Bioinformatics and Computational Biology</strong></strong></summary><!-- wp:list -->\n<ul><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Use of bioinformatics tools and high-performance computing systems and various computing support services to transform complex data into information useful to scientists</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list --></details>\n<!-- /wp:details -->\n\n<!-- wp:details {"showContent":true} -->\n<details class="wp-block-details" open><summary><strong>Molecular Diagnostic</strong></summary><!-- wp:list -->\n<ul><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Development of molecular tests, including biochemical, electrochemical, optical, and imaging-based, to diagnose diseases or other pathological conditions</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list --></details>\n<!-- /wp:details --></details>\n<!-- /wp:details -->\n\n<!-- wp:block {"ref":192} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:details -->\n<details class="wp-block-details"><summary><strong>TRAINING/ CONFERENCE VENUE</strong></summary><!-- wp:media-text {"mediaPosition":"right","mediaId":213,"mediaLink":"http://localhost/cbc-2021-9september-plenary-hall-audience-view-1/","mediaType":"image","verticalAlignment":"center","imageFill":true} -->\n<div class="wp-block-media-text has-media-on-the-right is-stacked-on-mobile is-vertically-aligned-center is-image-fill"><div class="wp-block-media-text__content"><!-- wp:paragraph {"placeholder":"Content…"} -->\n<p>Plenary Hall (Capacity:600 pax) </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><figure class="wp-block-media-text__media" style="background-image:url(http://localhost/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/CBC-2021-9September-Plenary-Hall-audience-view-1-1024x683.jpg);background-position:50% 50%"><img src="http://localhost/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/CBC-2021-9September-Plenary-Hall-audience-view-1-1024x683.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-213 size-full"/></figure></div>\n<!-- /wp:media-text -->\n\n<!-- wp:block {"ref":192} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:media-text {"mediaPosition":"right","mediaId":219,"mediaLink":"http://localhost/cbc-2021-9september-multipurpose-hall/","mediaType":"image","verticalAlignment":"center","imageFill":true} -->\n<div class="wp-block-media-text has-media-on-the-right is-stacked-on-mobile is-vertically-aligned-center is-image-fill"><div class="wp-block-media-text__content"><!-- wp:paragraph {"placeholder":"Content…"} -->\n<p>Multipurpose Hall (Сарасіtу: 300 рах)</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><figure class="wp-block-media-text__media" style="background-image:url(http://localhost/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/CBC-2021-9September-Multipurpose-Hall-1024x683.jpg);background-position:50% 50%"><img src="http://localhost/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/CBC-2021-9September-Multipurpose-Hall-1024x683.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-219 size-full"/></figure></div>\n<!-- /wp:media-text -->\n\n<!-- wp:block {"ref":192} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:media-text {"mediaPosition":"right","mediaId":215,"mediaLink":"http://localhost/cbc-2021-9september-office-1st-flr/","mediaType":"image","verticalAlignment":"center","imageFill":true} -->\n<div class="wp-block-media-text has-media-on-the-right is-stacked-on-mobile is-vertically-aligned-center is-image-fill"><div class="wp-block-media-text__content"><!-- wp:paragraph {"placeholder":"Content…"} -->\n<p>Training Rooms (Capacity: 300 pax)</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><figure class="wp-block-media-text__media" style="background-image:url(http://localhost/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/CBC-2021-9September-Office-1st-Flr-1024x461.jpg);background-position:50% 50%"><img src="http://localhost/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/CBC-2021-9September-Office-1st-Flr-1024x461.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-215 size-full"/></figure></div>\n<!-- /wp:media-text --></details>\n<!-- /wp:details -->\n\n<!-- wp:block {"ref":192} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:html -->\n<div class="relative mb-3">\n    <h6 class="mb-0">\n      <button\n        class="relative flex items-center w-full p-4 font-semibold text-left transition-all ease-in border-b border-solid cursor-pointer border-slate-100 text-slate-700 rounded-t-1 group text-dark-500"\n        data-collapse-target="collapse-1"\n      >\n        <span>What is Material Tailwind?</span>\n        <i class="absolute right-0 pt-1 text-xs fa fa-plus group-open:opacity-0"></i>\n        <i class="absolute right-0 pt-1 text-xs opacity-0 fa fa-minus group-open:opacity-100"></i>\n      </button>\n    </h6>\n    <div\n      data-collapse="collapse-1"\n      class="h-0 overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"\n    >\n      <div class="p-4 text-sm leading-normal text-blue-gray-500/80">\n        We\'re not always in the position that we want to be at. We\'re constantly\n        growing. We\'re constantly making mistakes. We\'re constantly trying to\n        express ourselves and actualize our dreams.\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class="relative mb-3">\n    <h6 class="mb-0">\n      <button\n        class="relative flex items-center w-full p-4 font-semibold text-left transition-all ease-in border-b border-solid cursor-pointer border-slate-100 text-slate-700 rounded-t-1 group text-dark-500"\n        data-collapse-target="collapse-2"\n      >\n        <span>How to use Material Tailwind?</span>\n        <i class="absolute right-0 pt-1 text-xs fa fa-plus group-open:opacity-0"></i>\n        <i class="absolute right-0 pt-1 text-xs opacity-0 fa fa-minus group-open:opacity-100"></i>\n      </button>\n    </h6>\n    <div\n      data-collapse="collapse-2"\n      class="h-0 overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"\n    >\n      <div class="p-4 text-sm leading-normal text-blue-gray-500/80">\n        We\'re not always in the position that we want to be at. We\'re constantly\n        growing. We\'re constantly making mistakes. We\'re constantly trying to\n        express ourselves and actualize our dreams.\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class="relative mb-3">\n    <h6 class="mb-0">\n      <button\n        class="relative flex items-center w-full p-4 font-semibold text-left transition-all ease-in border-b border-solid cursor-pointer border-slate-100 text-slate-700 rounded-t-1 group text-dark-500"\n        data-collapse-target="collapse-3"\n      >\n        <span>What can I do with Material Tailwind?</span>\n        <i class="absolute right-0 pt-1 text-xs fa fa-plus group-open:opacity-0"></i>\n        <i class="absolute right-0 pt-1 text-xs opacity-0 fa fa-minus group-open:opacity-100"></i>\n      </button>\n    </h6>\n    <div\n      data-collapse="collapse-3"\n      class="h-0 overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out"\n    >\n      <div class="p-4 text-sm leading-normal text-blue-gray-500/80">\n        We\'re not always in the position that we want to be at. We\'re constantly\n        growing. We\'re constantly making mistakes. We\'re constantly trying to\n        express ourselves and actualize our dreams.\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n<!-- /wp:html -->', 'What is DA-CBC?', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '152-revision-v1', '', '', '2024-05-28 11:29:57', '2024-05-28 03:2